        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): extract Undici cause.code for ECONNRESET/ECONNREFUSED/ETIMEDOUT",
        "body": "## Problem\nUndici wraps SocketError (ECONNRESET, ECONNREFUSED, ETIMEDOUT) in a cause chain. The current code in `extractTransportErrorDetails` reads `error.code`, `error.error`, and `error.errorCode`, but misses `error.cause.code` where these network error codes are actually stored.\n\n## Fix\nAdded `error.cause.code` as the final fallback in `extractTransportErrorDetails` before returning the raw error message. One line changed in production code.\n\n## Changes\n- `src/agents/transport-stream-shared.ts`: One-line addition — reads `error.cause.code` as final fallback, and exports `extractTransportErrorDetails` for testability\n- `src/agents/transport-stream-shared.test.ts`: 2 new unit tests\n  - Undici cause.code extraction test (simulates real Undici error shape)\n  - Priority verification (cause.code checked last, never shadows existing paths)\n\n## Testing\n- 24/24 tests passing (agents-core + agents-support)\n- New tests directly simulate the Undici error structure\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Undici Error Structure\n\nWhen `fetch()` fails with ECONNRESET against DeepSeek API, Undici produces:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": \"fetch failed\",\n  \"cause\": {\n    \"code\": \"ECONNRESET\",\n    \"errno\": -4077,\n    \"syscall\": \"read\"\n  },\n  \"name\": \"TypeError\"\n}\n```\n\nThe original code reads `error.code` and `error.error.code` — both `undefined` for this shape. The fix adds `error.cause.code` as the last fallback.\n\n### Unit Test Evidence (2026-07-18)\n\n```\n$ npx vitest run src/agents/transport-stream-shared.test.ts\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  24 passed (24)\n   Duration  3.60s\n```\n\nTwo new tests:\n\n1. **ECONNRESET extraction**: Input `{ message: \"fetch failed\", cause: { code: \"ECONNRESET\" } }` → output `errorCode: \"ECONNRESET\"` ✅\n2. **Priority preservation**: Input `{ errorCode: \"TOP_LEVEL\", code: \"MIDDLE\", cause: { code: \"CAUSE_CODE\" } }` → output `errorCode: \"TOP_LEVEL\"` ✅\n\n### Failover Chain Verification\n\n```\nextractTransportErrorDetails({ cause: { code: \"ECONNRESET\" } })\n  -> errorCode = \"ECONNRESET\"\n  -> classifyFailoverReasonFromCode(\"ECONNRESET\")  \n  -> ECONNRESET matches TIMEOUT_ERROR_CODES\n  -> classified as transient network failure\n  -> fallback to next provider triggered\n```\n\n## Risk\nExtremely low. One-line logic change, new code path only activates when existing fallbacks fail, no existing behavior modified.",
